The present invention relates to the field of methods and devices for measuring the status of oxidative stress on the surface or in a biological matrix. More particularly, it relates to a method for measuring the status of oxidative stress of a biological matrix involving at least one compound AB chosen fromNADH, NADPH, Cyt C ( SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1370.25 or H202.

The invention relates to the use of at least one compound AB which is non-toxic to the skin chosenfrom NADH, NADPH, Cyt C ( SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1370.25 or H202 for measuring the status of oxidative stress of a biologicalmatrix, characterized in that said at least one compound is available in two forms AB that do not interact with each other, and which are capable of interacting and/or forming complexes respectively with an antioxidant and an oxidant present on the surface or in said biological matrix.

For example, it is possible to use a group A comprising two compounds NAD* (0.1 M) and Cyt C Fe3 SVG
